# The shapes of the tokens that scripts/leak-scan finds in what a push would publish, and that the hooks leave out of
# .loop/blocks.log. Each line holds these fields, separated by tabs:
# - the kind of token
# - how many of a token's first characters the scan's findings show
# - the token's shape, which Python's re and grep -E read the same way
# - the characters that can't follow a token, as in a bracket expression, for a shape of a fixed length
# The scan counts a token only when no letter or digit comes just before it. The hooks leave out each word that holds
# a token's shape.
